.Dd July 19, 2026
.Dt SNAILRACE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm snailrace
.Nd benchmark commands: time, CPU, memory and disk footprint
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op options
.Fl -\ command
.Op Ar args ...
.Nm
.Op options
.Fl c Ar command
.Op Fl c Ar command
.Nm Cm tui
.Op options
.Fl -\ command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
benchmarks commands on Linux and macOS.
It measures wall-clock time, CPU usage, memory, process structure, and
static disk footprint, ranks the compared commands, and can save the
results as a report.
.Pp
Commands are given either after a
.Ql --
separator or with repeated
.Fl c
flags.
The
.Cm tui
subcommand renders a live terminal view while measuring.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss Input
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c , Fl command Ar string
Shell command to benchmark; repeat to compare several.
.It Fl label Ar string
Display label; repeat once per command, in order.
.It Fl prepare Ar string
One-time setup command run before measuring.
.El
.Ss Measurement
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n , Fl runs Ar int
Number of measured runs.
.It Fl warmups Ar int
Warmup runs per command.
.It Fl interval Ar duration
Process sampling interval.
.El
.Ss Ranking
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl index Ar list
Balanced index dimensions:
.Ql time ,
.Ql cpu ,
.Ql ram ,
.Ql disk .
.It Fl baseline Ar int
Baseline index; 0 selects the balanced winner.
.El
.Ss Output
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f , Fl format Ar list
Saved report format:
.Ql html ,
.Ql svg ,
.Ql markdown ,
.Ql json ,
.Ql text .
.It Fl o , Fl output Ar string
Directory for a saved report.
.It Fl verbose
Print full statistical tables to stdout.
.It Fl show-output
Forward command output to stderr.
.El
.Ss TUI ( Nm Cm tui No ... )
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d , Fl duration Ar duration
Fixed TUI measurement duration.
.It Fl width Ar uint
TUI columns; default inherits the terminal.
.It Fl height Ar uint
TUI rows; default inherits the terminal.
.El
.Ss Miscellaneous
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v , Fl version
Print version and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl help
Show help.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Benchmark one command with warmups:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
snailrace -n 20 -warmups 3 -- gzip -k sample.txt
.Ed
.Pp
Compare two commands and save an HTML report:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
snailrace -n 10 -f html -o report -c 'gzip -k sample.txt' -c 'zstd -k sample.txt'
.Ed
.Pp
Watch a command live in the TUI:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
snailrace tui -- make build
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
Project page:
.Lk https://github.com/shellcell/snailrace
